# Only debhelper is listed. The Rust toolchain is not taken from the archive:
# trixie ships rustc 1.85 but the crate is built against whatever stable
# rustup installs in the release container, and an archive-wide build-dep on
# "cargo" would pin the package to one release's toolchain. Build with
# "dpkg-buildpackage -d" so dpkg-checkbuilddeps does not object to a cargo
# that is on PATH but not dpkg-installed; see README.Debian.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/Alacrity-Education/microscope-importer

Package: microscope-importer
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         ffmpeg,
         udisks2,
         util-linux,
         fontconfig
Recommends: fonts-dejavu-core
Description: import footage from microscope SD cards and stitch video segments
 Microscope Importer is a terminal application that lists every SD card
 attached to the computer, mounted or not. Selecting a card imports all of
 its photos (jpg, jpeg, png) into ~/Pictures/Microscope and its videos (mp4)
 into ~/Videos/Microscope; several cards can be imported at the same time,
 each with its own progress bar, transfer rate and time estimate.
 .
 USB microscopes record in fixed segments of 1, 2, 3, 5, 10, 15 or 20
 minutes. The importer detects which segments belong to one recording (file
 counter, timestamps and stream parameters) and joins them back losslessly
 with ffmpeg, as a stream copy. Damaged segments are replaced by black video
 of the same length with a note naming the file, and the originals are kept
 in a hidden folder.
 .
 The card is unmounted as soon as everything is copied, so it can be taken
 out while the videos are still being stitched.
